The most recent version of the Volkswagen Transporter is the T6.1, although the new T7 Multivan has been introduced and a T7 Transporter is coming (Source 2, 10, 16, 18, 20, 23). The 'TDI' designation refers to the diesel engine type, and 'T30' refers to the 3000kg Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW). This is not a single trim level but a combination of engine type and GVW, available across various trims (Startline, Trendline, Highline, etc.). To provide a representative evaluation, I will focus on the characteristics common to a T30 TDI and assume a mid-range trim level (like Trendline or Commerce Plus), as this represents a typical configuration.

